    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0340" n="332" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4216a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-16T19:00:00-05:00">April 16, 1941—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>84. Your letter to the Under Secretary April 5.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d277-f1"/>
                    Please inform Lescot confidentially and unofficially that the Department plans
                    at an early date to propose the resumption of negotiations with his Government
                    looking toward a modification of the financial setup in Haiti including the
                    elimination of the office of Fiscal Representative.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
